+- Production code present: `js/app.js` and `index.html` implement the full TodoMVC spec.
+- External acceptance suite (Cypress) reports 10 failures — all originate from two product defects in `js/app.js`:
+  1. `render()` replaces all DOM nodes via `todoList.innerHTML = ''` on every state change, causing detached-node errors in a real browser.
+  2. The `dblclick` label handler sets `todo.editing = true` on the in-memory object but never calls `setTodos(todos)` before `render()`, so the editing state is lost when `render()` re-reads from localStorage. The `<li>` never gets `.editing` class, leaving the `.edit` input hidden (`display: none`).
 
 ## Decisions
 
 - Storage key: `todos-vanillajs` per spec convention (`todos-[framework]`).
 - Tier: happy-dom (default). The spec requires DOM rendering; happy-dom is the cheapest tier that observes it.
 - Scantling for localStorage shape at `scantlings/todo-storage.json`.
+- Conformance checks added under `features/dom-integrity.feature` to guard the anti-patterns happy-dom cannot detect.
 
